# Project Rules & Specification: Goal Ticker (Maritime Savings & Overtime PWA)

## 1. Project Overview
"Goal Ticker" is a mobile-first Progressive Web App (PWA) designed for a seafarer to visualize real-time savings toward specific material goals during a maritime contract. The core emotional and functional goal is to convert continuous 24/7 contract earnings into live, ticking progress bars for desired items, running 100% client-side with full offline support on iOS.

## 2. Complete Tech Stack & Libraries
- **Core Framework:** React 18+ with TypeScript (`strict` mode enabled).
- **Build Tool & Dev Server:** Vite (`npm run dev` on `localhost:5173` with HMR).
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS configured for iOS-native Dark Mode.
- **State Management & Persistence:** Zustand with `persist` middleware (storing all state, goals, and timestamp snapshots in `localStorage` so data survives app closures and background suspension on iOS).
- **Icons:** `lucide-react` (clean line icons for play/pause, navigation, checkmarks, and goal categories).
- **Celebration Effects:** `canvas-confetti` (with `@types/canvas-confetti`).
- **PWA & Offline Support:** `vite-plugin-pwa` (configured for iOS "Add to Home Screen" standalone mode and offline asset caching).
- **Unit Testing:** Vitest (used strictly for testing pure financial math, state transitions, and offline catch-up logic вЂ” NOT brittle UI layout tests).
- **Explicitly Excluded:** Zero external backend, zero REST/GraphQL APIs, zero external databases, and zero heavy third-party UI component libraries (no MUI, Chakra, or Ant Design).

## 3. UI/UX & Visual Architecture (iOS Dark Mode Reference)

### 3.1 Color Palette & Surfaces
- **Canvas Background:** Deep matte charcoal `#121212`.
- **Elevated Cards & Modals:** Dark slate `#1C1C1E` / `#242426` / `#2C2C2E` with subtle `1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06)` border and `rounded-2xl` (`16px`) corners.
- **Input Fields:** Recessed dark fill `#141416` or `#1C1C1E` inside modal cards (`rounded-xl`).
- **Primary Text:** Crisp White `#FFFFFF` (bold headings and primary dollar values).
- **Secondary / Muted Text:** Cool Gray `#8E8E93` (labels, subtitles, ETA text).
- **Active / Success Accent:** Vibrant Emerald Green #30D158 (primary CTA buttons, active progress bars, percentage readouts, bottom-anchored full-width CTA button). Text on emerald buttons must be high-contrast dark (#0A1F10 or #000000) bold for legibility.
- **Paused Accent:** Warm Amber `#FF9F0A` (paused pill badge, amber progress bar, "Resume Saving" CTA button).

### 3.2 Typography & Number Discipline
- **Font Family:** System UI (`-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "SF Pro Display", sans-serif`).
- **Tabular Numbers:** Every dynamic numeric readout (percentages, saved/target amounts, hourly/daily rates, ETA countdowns) MUST enforce `tabular-nums` (`font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`) to prevent horizontal layout jitter during 1-second updates.
- **Touch Targets:** All buttons, icon toggles, and tap targets must have a minimum height/width of `44px`.
- **UI Copy Tone (Strict Ban on Maritime / Nautical Terms):** All visible UI text, headings, labels, placeholders, and notifications MUST be neutral and finance/goal-focused. NEVER use maritime, nautical, or ship-related words or metaphors in the UI (strictly forbid phrases like "Welcome aboard", "contract", "voyage", "sail", "crew", "maritime", etc.).

### 3.3 Screen-by-Screen Layout Specifications

1. **Screen 1: Getting Started / Onboarding (`monthlySalary === 0`)**
   - Centered app title **`Goal Ticker`** in bold white at the upper-middle area.
   - Single elevated card (`#242426`, `rounded-2xl`, generous padding) containing:
     - Subtitle: *"Get started"*
     - Body copy: *"Set your monthly income to start tracking real-time savings toward your goals."*
   - Full-width primary emerald button (`#30D158`, `rounded-xl`, min-height `48px`): **`Set Monthly Salary`**.

2. **Screen 2: Set Salary Modal / View**
   - Centered elevated card (`#242426`, `rounded-2xl`) with title **`Contract Salary (USD)`**.
   - Large recessed numeric input box displaying a `$` prefix and prominent tabular value (e.g., `$ 3,500.00`).
   - Muted helper caption underneath: *"Enter your 30-day gross salary for accurate 24/7 accrual."*
   - Full-width emerald CTA button below the card: **`Save Salary`**.

3. **Screen 3: Active Goals Dashboard (Main View)**
   - **Header:** Bold left-aligned title **`Live Savings`** with a subtle secondary subtitle directly below showing current total earning speed (e.g., `Hourly Earning: $4.86`, calculated as `monthlySalary / (30 * 24)`). Tapping the header/rate opens the Set Salary view to edit salary.
   - **Goal Cards Stack (`gap-3`):** Each card (`#242426`, `rounded-2xl`, `p-4`, clickable to open Goal Detail) includes:
     - **Top Row:** Square rounded icon badge on the left (e.g., laptop/camera/target icon in subtle dark container), Goal Title (`New Laptop`) + muted `$1,800 / $4,200` readout in the middle, and a circular Pause/Play icon button (`44px` tap target, subtle emerald/amber/gray ring, `e.stopPropagation()`) on the right.
     - **Middle:** Horizontal progress bar (`h-2`, rounded-full, `#3A3A3C` track) filled with Emerald `#30D158` (when `active` or `completed`) or Amber `#FF9F0A` (when `paused`).
     - **Bottom Row:** Left-aligned green/amber percentage (`42.85%`) and right-aligned muted ETA (`ETA: 5d 11h 3m`, `Paused`, or `Completed`).
   - **Primary CTA Button:** Full-width rectangular button anchored at the bottom of the screen, matching goal-card horizontal width (w-full, px-4 horizontal padding, rounded-2xl, min-height 48px, vibrant emerald #30D158 background) with high-contrast dark bold text (#0A1F10) and + Add New Goal label; pinned to viewport bottom with pb-24 spacer on goals list so cards never overlap or hide behind the button at any scroll position.

4. **Screen 4: Goal Detail View (Opened on Card Tap)**
   - **Top Nav:** Left `<` back arrow (`44px` tap target) + centered title **`Goal Progress`**.
   - **Summary Card:** Goal title (`Camera Gear`) + inline pill badge (`PAUSED` in amber tint, `ACTIVE` in emerald tint, or `IDLE` in gray tint) + circular Play/Pause action button on the right.
   - **Progress Block:** `Saved` label, large bold `$760.00 / $5,000.00` counter, full-width progress bar (Amber when paused, Emerald when active), `Progress` label on the left, and percentage (`15.20%`) on the right.
   - **Stats Breakdown Card:** Clean key-value rows:
     - `Daily Rate:` (current active share per 24h, e.g., `$1.21`, or `$0.00` when paused/idle)
     - `Started:` (formatted creation/start date, e.g., `12 Sep 2025`)
     - `Target:` (`$5,000.00`)
   - **Bottom Actions:** Full-width primary button вЂ” Amber **`Resume Saving`** (`#FF9F0A`) when paused, Emerald **`Start Saving`** when idle, or subtle **`Pause Saving`** when active, plus a discreet **`Delete Goal`** button below.

5. **Screen 5: Completed Goal Achieved Modal / Celebration State**
   - Subtle `canvas-confetti` celebration burst when a goal transitions to `completed` (`100.00%`).
   - Header **`Goal Achieved!`** with a dark celebration card containing:
     - Goal title (`Sony A7 IV`) and a circular emerald checkmark badge (`#30D158`) on the right.
     - Full `100.00%` emerald progress bar with centered percentage label.
     - `Saved` label and matching `$4,200.00 / $4,200.00` readout.
     - Congratulatory note: *"Congratulations! You've saved up for this goal during your contract."*
   - Two stacked bottom buttons:
     - Secondary outlined dark button: **`Share Achievement`** (copies formatted achievement summary to clipboard or triggers Web Share API).
     - Primary emerald button: **`Start a New Goal`** (closes modal / opens Create New Goal).

6. **Screen 6: Create New Goal Modal / Screen**
   - Header with close/back action and title **`Add New Goal`**.
   - **Goal Name** input (`#1C1C1E`, `rounded-xl`, placeholder e.g., `Vacation Fund`).
   - **Target Amount (USD)** numeric input with `$` prefix (e.g., `$ 2,500`).
   - **Logic Alignment Note:** All `active` goals split `baseRatePerMs` equally (`baseRatePerMs / N`). Do NOT introduce weighted priority multipliers that break equal splitting.
   - Full-width emerald CTA button at the bottom: **`Create Goal`**.

## 4. Core Business Logic & Math Model (CRITICAL)
1. **Continuous 24/7 Rate:**
   - User inputs their 30-day salary in USD (`monthlySalary`).
   - Base earning rate per millisecond:
     `baseRatePerMs = monthlySalary / (30 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000)`
2. **Parallel Goal Splitting:**
   - Multiple goals can be in the `active` state simultaneously.
   - `baseRatePerMs` is split **equally** among all currently `active` goals (`N`).
   - Speed per active goal = `baseRatePerMs / N` (when `N > 0`).
   - Goals in `idle`, `paused`, or `completed` states receive `0` rate.
3. **Timestamp-Based Persistence (No Background Timers for Accrual):**
   - iOS suspends PWA background threads. NEVER rely on `setInterval` increments for actual financial accumulation.
   - Store `accumulatedAmount` (in USD) per goal and `lastUpdatedTimestamp` (`Date.now()`).
   - **Settle Before Mutation:** Whenever a state transition occurs (Start, Pause, Resume, Add Goal, Delete Goal, Salary Change), first settle/commit the earned amounts up to `Date.now()` before changing active goal counts or rates.
   - **Auto-Completion Cascade (Offline Catch-up):** When calculating elapsed time `deltaMs = now - lastUpdatedTimestamp`, check if any active goal reaches 100% (`targetAmount`) *before* `now`. If Goal A finishes at `t_finish < now`, cap Goal A at `targetAmount` (`status: 'completed'`), reduce active count `N - 1`, and apply the newly freed rate to the remaining active goals for the remaining time `now - t_finish`. Repeat iteratively until `now` is reached or `N === 0`.
4. **Goal Lifecycle States:**
   - `idle`: Created, `0%` progress, shows "Start Saving" action.
   - `active`: Ticking live every second on UI (`2` decimal places on percentage, e.g., `42.85%`), shows progress bar, saved/remaining USD, and dynamic ETA (`Xd Yh Zm`), shows "Pause" action.
   - `paused`: Frozen progress in amber (`#FF9F0A`), shows "Resume" action.
   - `completed`: Reached `100.00%`, locked at `targetAmount`, triggers `canvas-confetti` once upon completion/discovery, shows Goal Achieved view / completed badge.

## 5. Coding Rules & Incremental Workflow for VS Code Agent
- **Strict One-Step Execution:** Implement ONLY the single step explicitly requested by the user. Never jump ahead, scaffold future features, or refactor unrelated files.
- **Clean Architecture:** Keep pure math and cascade simulation isolated in `src/utils/calculator.ts`, formatting helpers in `src/utils/formatters.ts`, state persistence in `src/store/useGoalStore.ts`, and UI components in `src/components/`.
- **Test Discipline:** Write Vitest unit tests ONLY for `src/utils/calculator.ts` and store state transitions (covering 0 active goals, equal splitting, pause/resume settlement, and multi-goal cascade completion). Do not write UI/DOM snapshot tests.
- **Verification Before Completion:** After every step, ensure TypeScript compiles cleanly (`npx tsc --noEmit`) and all existing Vitest tests pass (`npx vitest run`) before finishing the turn.
- **Language:** All code, file names, comments, variable names, and UI copy must be in clean, idiomatic English.

## 6. - **Semantic Versioning:** Track the app version starting at `1.0` for the next release commit, and increment it logically with every subsequent feature commit/deployment (`1.1`, `1.2`, or `2.0` for major updates).
- **Single Source of Truth:** Always update the `"version"` field in `package.json` (and `manifest` / app config if applicable) before committing.
- **Visible UI Version Tag:** Display the current app version subtly in the UI (e.g., top-right of the dashboard header as `v1.0`) so the user can visually verify that the installed iOS PWA has updated to the latest deployed build.
- **Git Tagging & Commit Messages:** Include the version number in the commit message (e.g., `chore(release): bump version to v1.0 - ...`) and create an annotated Git tag (`git tag v1.0`) pushed along with `origin main`.

## 7. Git & GitHub Repository Workflow
- **Remote Repository URL:** `https://github.com/danil-droider/TOLSFTI-2.0.git`
- **Explicit Trigger Only:** NEVER run `git commit` or `git push` automatically after completing a coding step unless the user explicitly asks to commit and push.
- **Repository Setup (On First Push Request):**
  - Check if Git is initialized (`git status`). If not, run `git init`, create a clean `.gitignore` (excluding `node_modules`, `dist`, `.env`, and local logs), and set the default branch to `main` (`git branch -M main`).
  - Ensure the `origin` remote points to `https://github.com/danil-droider/TOLSFTI-2.0.git` (`git remote add origin https://github.com/danil-droider/TOLSFTI-2.0.git` or `git remote set-url origin ...`).
- **Commit & Push Procedure:**
  - Verify `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npx vitest run` (if tests exist) pass before committing.
  - Stage all relevant project changes (`git add .`), create a clear, descriptive English commit message reflecting the completed step (e.g., `feat: complete step 1 onboarding and salary screens`), and push to `origin main` (`git push -u origin main`).




